  {
   "id": 646796,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<p>Examine the solution method that has been started below and use it to answer the remaining three parts of question 1.</p>\n\n<blockquote>\n<p>Original equation<br> <span data-math=\"x^2+7x+10=0\">x^2+7x+10=0</span></p>\n<p><strong>Step 1</strong> - Subtract 10 from each side.<br> <span data-math=\"x^2+7x=-10\">x^2+7x=-10</span></p>\n<p><strong>Step 2</strong> - Multiply each side by 4.<br> <span data-math=\"4x^2+4(7x)=-4(10)\">4x^2+4(7x)=-4(10)</span></p>\n<p><strong>Step 3</strong> - Rewrite <span data-math=\"4x^2\">4x^2</span> as <span data-math=\"(2x)^2\">(2x)^2</span> and <span data-math=\"4(7x)\">4(7x)</span> as <span data-math=\"2(7)2x\">2(7)2x</span>.<br> <span data-math=\"(2x)^2+2(7)(2x) +\\_\\_\\_\\_^2=\\_\\_\\_\\_^2-4(10)\">(2x)^2+2(7)(2x) +\\_\\_\\_\\_^2=\\_\\_\\_\\_^2-4(10)</span></p>\n<p><strong>Step 4</strong> - <span data-math=\"\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\">\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_</span><br> <span data-math=\"(2x+\\_\\_\\_\\_)^2=\\_\\_\\_\\_^2-4(10)\">(2x+\\_\\_\\_\\_)^2=\\_\\_\\_\\_^2-4(10)</span></p>\n<p><strong>Step 5</strong> - <span data-math=\"\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\">\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_</span><br> <span data-math=\"2x+\\_\\_\\_\\_= \\pm \\sqrt{\\_\\_\\_\\_^2-4(10)}\">2x+\\_\\_\\_\\_= \\pm \\sqrt{\\_\\_\\_\\_^2-4(10)}</span></p>\n<p><strong>Step 6</strong> - <span data-math=\"\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\">\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_</span><br> <span data-math=\"2x=\\_\\_\\_\\_\\pm \\sqrt{\\_\\_\\_\\_^2-4(10)}\">2x=\\_\\_\\_\\_\\pm \\sqrt{\\_\\_\\_\\_^2-4(10)}</span></p>\n<p><strong>Step 7</strong> - <span data-math=\"\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\">\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_</span><br> <span data-math=\"x= \\_\\_\\_\\_\">x= \\_\\_\\_\\_</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n\n<ol class=\"os-raise-noindent\" start=\"4\" type=\"a\">\n  <li>In Step 2, what might be a good reason for multiplying each side of the equation by 4?</li>\n</ol>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1273393,
     "content_html": "Multiplying by 4 makes the coefficient of the squared term a perfect square, which makes it easier to complete the square."
    },
    {
     "id": 1273394,
     "content_html": "Multiplying by 4 makes the coefficient of the <span data-math=\"b\">b</span> term a perfect square, which makes it easier to complete the square."
    },
    {
     "id": 1273395,
     "content_html": "If the value of <span data-math=\"c\">c</span> is positive and you multiply by 4, it will be easier to divide the <span data-math=\"b\">b</span> term by 3 before you square it."
    },
    {
     "id": 1273396,
     "content_html": "You must always multiply both sides by 4 when completing the square."
    }
   ],
